    LLM: 'Game: Taroky Nebraska. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Nebraska Taroky is a four-player trick-taking game played mainly by people of Czech descent in Nebraska. 54-card Tarok pack: 22 trumps (Skies/Å kÃ½z highest, then 21 down to 1) and four suits of 8. Play is clockwise (unlike European Taroky). Bidder chooses partner by calling a King (not trump XIX). Object: win tricks with valuable cards. Follow suit; trump if void. Count cards in packets of three, subtract 2 per packet. Bonuses for declared combinations. Typically played for money with settlements after each hand.',
    objective: 'Win tricks with valuable cards; bidder chooses partner by calling a King. Count cards in packets of three, subtract 2 per packet. Bonuses for declared combinations.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal: 12 cards each, 6 in blind. 2. Bidding; bidder calls a King for partner (not trump XIX). 3. Play 12 tricks clockwise; follow suit, trump if void. 4. Score: count cards in packets of three, subtract 2 per packet; bonuses for declared combinations. Settlements after each hand.',
